1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 20702, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01UBR6GPUj4qD4jPBh3XBg3o", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20702, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01MpDqrxhovdrjz8ZKvSDqup", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 21002, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01MpDqrxhovdrjz8ZKvSDqup", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 21002, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01MpDqrxhovdrjz8ZKvSDqup", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 25950, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_014KgPpkaJuKArRBf1ynavYL", "tool": "create_incident", "args": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollback in all regions. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (and why it went to production even though the RC was unhealthy in staging), and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout partway.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 56550, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014KgPpkaJuKArRBf1ynavYL", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56550, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014KgPpkaJuKArRBf1ynavYL", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58466, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01XftBUc8Z13tepoxLGvhwgs", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 58766, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01XftBUc8Z13tepoxLGvhwgs", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 58766, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01XftBUc8Z13tepoxLGvhwgs", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 63865, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The failing v2.3.1 is on top of it, and its release candidate had also failed health checks in staging.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I retried once, and that updated all regions.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Rather than retry and risk a duplicate page, I checked the incident list and confirmed it had been created. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current state.\n\nINC-0001 lists two follow-ups:\n- Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and why it went to production even though its release candidate failed in staging.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback partway.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016xvm7oWBM8FH16CNoJbBWN", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01SzgBS3QpSd3eZJJs13iM6g", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_017zrW69yEiUDwUkE7EAvywh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NNdS9ZgRHPiKtioC3hm36T", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback stopped partway: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version again is safe to repeat, so I'll retry once.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01Livhu63oYEjaqR3cze3m9e", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01UBR6GPUj4qD4jPBh3XBg3o", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01MpDqrxhovdrjz8ZKvSDqup", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014KgPpkaJuKArRBf1ynavYL", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2013 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After the v2.3.1 deploy, checkout-api failed health checks in all production regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging. I rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the regions on mixed versions. A retry finished the rollback in all regions. All regions are now on v2.3.0, the service reports healthy, and the error rate is about 0.2%. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (and why it went to production even though the RC was unhealthy in staging), and look into the orchestrator error that stopped the rollout partway.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01XftBUc8Z13tepoxLGvhwgs", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened a SEV2 incident, INC-0001, which paged on-call.\n\n- **Version chosen:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production. The failing v2.3.1 is on top of it, and its release candidate had also failed health checks in staging.\n- **Rollback:** The first attempt stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1. Rolling back to the same version is safe to repeat, so I retried once, and that updated all regions.\n- **Current state:** us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0. The service reports healthy, and the error rate dropped from about 18% to about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Rather than retry and risk a duplicate page, I checked the incident list and confirmed it had been created. It describes the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and the current state.\n\nINC-0001 lists two follow-ups:\n- Find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure, and why it went to production even though its release candidate failed in staging.\n- Look into the orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback partway.", "type": "text"}]}]}